 ("infrastructure", "n.", "基礎設施、基礎建設", "The city will spend two billion dollars upgrading its transportation infrastructure.", "市政府將投入二十億美元升級交通基礎建設。"),
 ("inherent", "adj.", "固有的、內在的", "There are risks inherent in expanding into unfamiliar foreign markets.", "進軍陌生的海外市場本身就存在風險。"),
 ("insight", "n.", "洞察、深入了解", "The survey results gave us valuable insight into customer buying habits.", "調查結果讓我們深入了解顧客的購買習慣。"),
 ("inspection", "n.", "檢查、檢驗", "The building must pass a fire safety inspection before it can open to the public.", "大樓必須通過消防安全檢查才能對外開放。"),
 ("installment", "n.", "分期付款（的一期）", "Customers can pay for the furniture in twelve monthly installments with no interest.", "顧客可以分十二期免息支付家具款項。"),
 ("instrumental", "adj.", "起關鍵作用的", "Ms. Haddad was instrumental in securing the contract with the government agency.", "Haddad 女士在拿下這份政府機構合約上居功厥偉。"),
 ("insufficient", "adj.", "不足的", "The payment was declined due to insufficient funds in the account.", "因帳戶餘額不足，該筆付款遭拒。"),
 ("intellectual property", "n.", "智慧財產", "Our legal team works to protect the company's intellectual property in overseas markets.", "我們的法務團隊致力於保護公司在海外市場的智慧財產。"),
 ("intensive", "adj.", "密集的", "New pilots must complete an intensive three-week training program before their first flight.", "新進飛行員在首次飛行前，必須完成為期三週的密集訓練課程。"),
 ("interim", "adj.", "臨時的、代理的", "Mr. Ito will serve as interim director until a permanent replacement is found.", "在找到正式人選前，Ito 先生將擔任代理主任。"),
 ("irrespective of", "phr.", "不論、不管", "All staff receive the same training, irrespective of their previous experience.", "不論過去經驗如何，所有員工都接受相同的訓練。"),
